@startuml STM-6_FaultEvent
!include _style.iuml
title STM-6 FaultEvent (operator alert)\nfault_events.status · v0.2 · 24/10/2026 · trigger names from WP4 FaultStateMachine (Nghĩa)
[*] --> raised : SIGNAL\n[driver report, Faulted status\nor pillar offline past alert delay]\n/ hide connector, notify operator
raised --> acknowledged : ACKNOWLEDGE (Operator)
raised --> resolved : CONNECTOR_AVAILABLE
acknowledged --> resetting : RESET_SENT (Operator remote reset)\n/ start reset timer
resetting --> resolved : CONNECTOR_AVAILABLE
resetting --> acknowledged : RESET_FAILED\n(refused or reset timeout)
acknowledged --> resolved : CONNECTOR_AVAILABLE or\nOPERATOR_CLOSE after site visit
resolved --> [*]
note right of acknowledged
  One open FaultEvent per connector.
  Maintenance tickets are Should (FR-18).
  CONNECTOR_AVAILABLE = connector works again:
  Available or straight to Preparing / Charging /
  Suspended / Finishing / Reserved (not Unavailable).
end note
@enduml